@issue-278 @bug @delivery @versioning
Feature: Synchronize delivery versions from project steering
  The v3 delivery controller must preserve automated release behavior while
  updating the native version artifacts declared by each project's technical steering.

  Scenario: Python project delivers without Node metadata
    Given a project has VERSION and CHANGELOG.md
    And technical steering declares pyproject.toml field project.version
    And technical steering declares src/pennyscan/__init__.py field __version__
    And the project has no package.json
    When the v3 delivery controller computes a release version
    Then VERSION contains the release version
    And pyproject.toml project.version contains the release version
    And src/pennyscan/__init__.py __version__ contains the release version
    And CHANGELOG.md contains the release entry
    And no package.json is read or created

  Scenario: Node project keeps its declared package mirror
    Given technical steering declares package.json field version
    And package.json version equals VERSION
    When the v3 delivery controller computes a release version
    Then package.json version contains the release version
    And the remaining JSON document stays valid

  Scenario Outline: Invalid declared mirror stops delivery
    Given technical steering declares a stack-specific version mirror
    And the declared mirror is <condition>
    When the v3 delivery controller attempts synchronization
    Then delivery writes a failed handoff
    And no delivery commit is created
    And no pull request is opened

    Examples:
      | condition |
      | missing |
      | not synchronized with VERSION |
      | outside the repository root |
      | ambiguous at its text field locator |

  Scenario: Resume requires every configured artifact
    Given a prior delivery commit contains a matching changelog release entry
    And technical steering declares Python version mirrors
    When a configured mirror is absent from that commit
    Then the prior delivery state is not considered synchronized
    And delivery does not skip artifact synchronization

  Scenario: Stack-agnostic synchronization preserves v3 delivery
    Given every configured version artifact is synchronized
    When the v3 controller continues delivery
    Then semver classification and approved-major enforcement are unchanged
    And automated review remediation is unchanged
    And exact-head merge and issue closure proof are unchanged
